"""
HELPS = {
    "add": """aos-tools add - register a tool in the registry or overlay

usage: aos-tools [--file F] [--overlay O] add [--override] [--name N] [--no-cache]
               [--env-file FILE] [--envs K=V]... (XXX | --path-json JSON)

XXX is a folder, JSON file or executable, relative to cwd. Prints added NAME -> PATH
with an absolute path. The stored path keeps your form: an absolute XXX is stored
absolute; a relative XXX is stored relative to the directory of the file written (the
overlay with --overlay, else the registry). --path-json stores JSON as given: a path
string or a directive such as {"$env": "AOS_PROTO8", "$path": "/lib/base/bash"},
resolved on every use (relative results from that same directory), never written back.
Names default to the folder name or file name without extension;
only [A-Za-z0-9_-] is accepted, at most 64 characters.

flags:
      --file F      registry file before add (default: ./tools.json)
      --overlay O   overlay before add; write only this overlay
      --override    replace an existing name
  -n, --name N      register under this name
      --no-cache    disable executable --tooldef caching (executables only)
      --path-json J store this JSON path value (string or directive) instead of XXX
